"answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative launched in June with an initial budget of $500,000, led by Sarah Tan. The project has since expanded its budget to $550,000 to accommodate real-time analytics integration and team expansion, welcoming Mike Chen and Lisa Ray. Key developments include initial findings suggesting a 20% efficiency increase via AI algorithms, a partnership with TechInnovate for AI technology, and the achievement of a major milestone with a successfully tested secure file sharing prototype. Phase Two has seen breakthroughs in predictive analytics, with further updates scheduled for staff meetings in August, October, and November."
